  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r \rLocation Plan Dated 07.04.2026 \rSite Block Plan Cycle and Waste Storage Romeo PL02 Dated 17.03.2026\rPre Existing Floor Plans Dated Romeo-PL03 Dated 17.03.2026\rExisting and Proposed Floor Plans Elevations and Sections Romeo PL01 Dated 17.03.2026\rDesign and Access Planning Statement;\rFlood Risk Assessment;\rSheffield Stand Specification Sheet;\rFire Statement;\rHighway Safety Impact Form;\rSuDS Pro Forma;\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the approved plans and supporting information, the development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than FIVE residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, cycle parking shall be provided on site in compliance with the following criteria:\r\ri) Provision of a minimum of FIVE long stay cycle parking spaces\r\rii) In an accessible location; the access route to each long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates [excluding the store door] which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m.\r\riii) Secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob.\r\riv) Fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rSuch facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, details of the design of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r"
  ],
